{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.NormalForm","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.Order","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.norm_le_of_bounded_on_punctured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.norm_le_of_bounded_on_punctured","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.lean#L64-L79","doc":"**Punctured-bounded everywhere ⇒ globally bounded** (normal form). If a meromorphic\nnormal-form function `g` on `ℂ` is bounded by `C` on a punctured neighborhood of *every* point,\nthen `‖g z‖ ≤ C` for every `z`: order ≥ 0 (previous lemma) makes each point a removable\nsingularity, so `g` is analytic — hence continuous — at `z`, and its value is the limit of the\n(bounded) nearby values. This turns a codiscrete (dense-complement) bound into the global\n`hbdd` the boundedness capstone requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_of_bounded_punctured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_of_bounded_punctured","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeromorphicPuncturedBounded.lean#L39-L62","doc":"**Local bounded ⇒ order ≥ 0.** A bound on a *punctured neighborhood* `𝓝[≠] z` alone\nforces `meromorphicOrderAt f z ≥ 0`: a negative-order point would send `f → ∞` on `𝓝[≠] z`\n(`tendsto_cobounded_of_meromorphicOrderAt_neg`), but the bound keeps `f` inside a ball there —\nand `𝓝[≠] z` is `NeBot`, so it cannot simultaneously be eventually-in and eventually-out. This\nis the punctured-neighborhood strengthening of\n`BoundedMeromorphicLiouville.meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_of_bounded` (which assumes a global\nbound). ","signatureChunk":0}]}